<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soweto uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soweto uprising began on 16 June 1976, when thousands of Black schoolchildren in Soweto, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>, marched against the compulsory use of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> as a language of instruction. Police opened fire, killing Hector Pieterson among others, and protests spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, leaving several hundred people dead in the following months. The uprising revived internal resistance to apartheid, and 16 June is now Youth Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soweto-uprising.jpg" alt="Soweto uprising" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sam Nzima · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mbuyisa_Makhubu_carries_Hector_Pieterson_at_Soweto_Uprising.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
